  "readings": [
    {
      "id": "U5L-READ-1",
      "title": "My First Talent Show",
      "text": "Last month, our school put up a notice about a talent show in the hall. I felt some anxiety at first, because I am always nervous in front of people. My friend Amy helped me pick a song, and we had to sit up late every night to practice. She saved all our songs in a class album. On the show day, the lobby was full of parents. A heavy box blocked the door, so we tried to pick up the box together. Someone forgot to turn on the bright lights, and I waited alone on the stage. But my loneliness went away when the music started. The judges said my voice was notable. One of them was a noble singer who told me that music is a language of the heart. Now I know that practice can discover something new in anyone."
    }
  ],
